cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use esis in your research, please cite it using these metadata, along with the ESIS mission paper listed in the references."
type: software
title: esis
abstract: >-
  esis is a Python library for modeling and interpreting observations from the
  EUV Snapshot Imaging Spectrograph (ESIS), a NASA sounding rocket mission
  which measures the speed of plasma in the solar atmosphere. It provides a
  model of the ESIS optical system built on optika, and a pipeline which
  reduces the images captured during flight to physically meaningful
  quantities. It is published on PyPI as euv-snapshot-imaging-spectrograph.
